// FarmLedger - How a farmer gets insured and paid
// Eraser: New diagram > "Sequence" > paste
title From sign-up to payout
autoNumber on

Farmer [icon: user, color: green]
Agent [icon: user, color: blue]
Insurance company [icon: briefcase, color: blue]
Vet [icon: activity, color: blue]
FarmLedger [icon: shield, color: purple]
Weather data [icon: sun, color: orange]
Mobile Money [icon: dollar-sign, color: orange]

Farmer > FarmLedger: Signs up by phone or website
FarmLedger > Agent: Assigns a local agent
Agent > FarmLedger: Applies for insurance with the farmer
FarmLedger > Insurance company: Sends application for review
Insurance company > FarmLedger: Approves and prepares an offer
FarmLedger > Farmer: Text: your offer is ready
Farmer > Mobile Money: Pays (government covers part of the cost)
Mobile Money > FarmLedger: Payment confirmed
FarmLedger > Farmer: Text: you are insured

Weather data > FarmLedger: Regular rainfall and crop health readings

alt [label: crops, bad weather detected, color: green] {
  FarmLedger > Mobile Money: Pays the farmer automatically
}
else [label: cattle or other loss, farmer reports it, color: blue] {
  Farmer > FarmLedger: Reports the loss
  alt [label: cattle] {
    FarmLedger > Vet: Vets check the claim
    Vet > FarmLedger: Claim confirmed
  }
  else [label: crop loss] {
    FarmLedger > Insurance company: Insurer staff check the claim
    Insurance company > FarmLedger: Claim confirmed
  }
  FarmLedger > Mobile Money: Pays the farmer
}

Mobile Money > Farmer: Money received
FarmLedger > Farmer: Text: payout sent
